invariant: INV-17
file: quic_fail.c
catches: quic_driver_test
reason: quic_wipe_write_keys zeroes a level's write keys and leaves its
  write bit set, so ch_quic_seal_close admits a second packet at a level
  that already sent its close, sealed under zero keys. The write bit is
  what refuses the second call, and test_close_after_failure requires
  CH_EINVAL from it at the Initial and the Handshake level.

--- old
    q->levels_ready &= (uint8_t)~CH_QUIC_LEVEL_BIT(level, CH_KEY_WRITE);
}
--- new
}
